## Coal Plant Boss

Dumb, corrupt head of the coal plant. Uneducated about science but latches onto "cancer research" as a PR opportunity for his struggling plant. Becomes a comedic obstacle by drawing too much attention to the lab team. (human)

The boss once tried to integrate robots into the plant for efficiency. It failed — "they couldn't handle the smoke." This shows the boss is not a stranger to wild, unconventional ideas for improving the plant; he's open to harebrained schemes, which makes his embrace of the "cancer research" cover story feel consistent with his character. (human)

Scene: The boss drops in to check on the "cancer research." Scientists hedge — "these things take a long time..." He cuts them off with a wink and a nudge: "Showing signs of progress... right!" He leaves satisfied, having manufactured the soundbite he needed. (human)
